WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.590
So, even with a design system in hand,

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.390
we're actually not stopping there. What

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.470
we are going to do now is to make it

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.710
even more visually stunning. And there

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.270
are a couple ways to do this, so I'll

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.070
break this down into different modules

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.270
so that you can get more techniques in

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.630
order to build out amazing front ends

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.510
that will put you leagues ahead of

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.030
everyone else. For this module in

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.670
particular, what I'll teach you is this

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.190
technique called UI sniping. And one of

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.990
the best references that you can

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.830
bookmark right now is this website

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.310
called 21st.dev, which I'll link below.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.190
And what this basically does is it

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.430
allows you to browse a lot of

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.750
well-built, already pre-built components

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.430
for your website. To give an example,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.230
there is this 3D robot view. If you

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.350
need, let's say, a globe animation that

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.270
is also available here. There's a lot of

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.990
components around buttons if you're

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.630
developing applications. And the way to

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.990
add this to your website is really,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.230
really easy because, let's say, if I

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.990
just go and search for, let's say,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.790
testimonial components in here. So,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.590
we'll be able to browse a few of these,

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.950
and I think the one that would be good

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.750
for our website, let's see. Let's

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.430
actually use this one. So, let's say we

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.350
want to include this component in the

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.430
Agency X website that we just built.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.150
What I'll just do, copy this prompt.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.030
I'll go back to our session, and what I

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.550
want to do is just paste that whole

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.030
thing, and just give Claude a task, and

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.990
I'll say, "Please include this as part

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.990
of the website." And let's say, "Select

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.870
an appropriate section or place of the

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.430
website to put this in, and make sure to

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.630
adopt the design system we already did.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.030
So, if we send over that prompt, then

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.510
Claude will basically just add in that

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.030
testimonial component into our website.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.670
So, now if we go back to our website and

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.190
scroll down, we should now see our

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.710
testimonial page at the bottom here. So,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.070
not only is it able to add it in, it was

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.030
also able to adopt the design to the

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.110
system that we set it for. And so, that

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.070
is the power of UI sniping. With

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.150
21st.dev, you can just find any of the

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.550
components here that are being shared by

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.590
the world, and you can just plug them

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.870
into your websites or builds. Now, let's

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.670
take this further because as you browse

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.390
the web, you may find some design

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.469
inspirations as well that you want to be

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:05.270
able to emulate in Claude. So, how do

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.910
you do that if it's not available in a

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.029
template website like 21st.dev? Well,

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.550
it's pretty simple if you have the tool

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.710
that I'll show you now. Basically, if

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.710
you go to any website, I like this one

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.350
called recent.design because it's

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.670
constantly updated with nice websites in

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.949
here which have really good design

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:22.870
principles. And there's other websites

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.990
like this, I'll give links down below so

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.510
that you can bookmark them and get a lot

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.790
of inspiration when it comes to

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.630
front-end building. But let's say we

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.350
like this website in particular, and

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.310
this is the business website of X.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.790
Namely, what we want here is this nice

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.230
animation in the middle. So, what I

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.110
built for us is this Chrome extension

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.750
which if you click on that, you can see

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.630
it opens up this Robo Capture window for

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.310
me. And what that allows me to do is to

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.550
just get the component of the website

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.470
that I want to get from this page. So,

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.870
let's say I want this SVG block, I just

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.470
click on that and that will store that

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.270
in this window. If I want another

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.150
section in here, I can just continuously

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.470
add and snipe those UI elements. But

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.750
obviously, I only want this SVG block,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.710
so I'll just remove this. And once I've

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.270
picked everything that I need, I can

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.990
just click on copy and I'll just go back

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.630
to Claude and give it that piece of

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.509
script. And now, what I want to do is

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:14.630
I'll just say, "Hey Claude, so what I

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.990
want to do is take a look at this

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.630
component and I want you to apply it to

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.390
our website. So, it's going to be an

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.949
animation of how we actually build

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:27.030
agents. So, please use this as a design

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.350
inspiration and build it out according

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.030
to our design system as appropriate for

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.150
Agency X." So, I'll just send that over

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.990
and let's see what Claude will do with

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.509
that. Now, this Chrome extension, I just

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:39.390
built it out and I'll link it down below

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.430
so that you can grab it as well. If in

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:42.630
case you haven't installed a Chrome

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.390
extension before in your local device,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.270
this is actually good practice because

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.310
with Chrome, the great thing about it is

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.910
Claude is really good at creating Chrome

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.870
extensions. And if you go to this URL,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.430
chrome: //extensions,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.830
and just toggle developer mode as on. If

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.030
you click load unpacked and point it to

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.910
the folder where you downloaded that

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.710
RoboCapture Chrome extension, then that

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.630
should now load that extension for you

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.470
to use. And now once it's done, let's

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.710
just scroll down and there you go. So,

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.390
this whole animation, this whole

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.310
component, we just created it by using a

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.349
reference, pointing RoboCapture to it,

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:19.430
and just giving it to Claude. So, now it

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.509
has this section, every agent drawn to

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:23.670
spec, that gives the complete steps,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.360
let's say, for Agency X to do its work.
